    </p>
    <p class="px-4 py-2 text-primary text-sm leading-relaxed flex flex-row gap-x-2">
      <img src="https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/e/notoemoji/16.0/270d_fe0f/72.png" width="16px" alt="">Autora: María Alejandra Olarte Molina
    </p>
    ):(
    <h2 class="my-2 p-4 font-bold">Winner of the Creative Writing Contest for Migrants in New Zealand</h2>
    <p class="px-4 py-2 text-primary text-sm leading-relaxed">
      With great joy, we announce the winner of our Creative Writing Contest for Migrants in New Zealand: <strong>María Alejandra Olarte Molina</strong>, author of the short story <i>“Al otro lado del mundo”</i>.
    </p>
    <p class="flex justify-center">
      <img src="/images/news/MariaAlejandraOlarteMolina.webp" alt="Maria Olarte - Ganadora del Concurso de Escritura Creativa para Personas Migrantes en Nueva Zelanda" class="my-4 rounded-sm" />
    </p>
    <p class="px-4 py-2 text-primary text-sm leading-relaxed">
      In her text, María Alejandra invites us to journey through the intimate and profound experience of migration—one that is not always measured in kilometers, but in affection, memories, and lessons learned. With an honest and sensitive voice, she reminds us that <i>“living in another country and inhabiting a language that is not the one of your birthplace is a daily exercise in courage”</i>, and that the hardest part is not the accent, but being far from your roots, from “the people who name your story”.
    </p>
    <p class="px-4 py-2 text-primary text-sm leading-relaxed">
From New Zealand, María Alejandra rebuilds her life between two geographies, celebrating the everyday, redefining success, and learning to be grateful even through nostalgia. Her story speaks of family love, emotional well-being, the strength needed to begin again, and the beauty that emerges when one lives “Al otro lado del mundo” with open eyes.
    </p>
    <p class="px-4 py-2 text-primary text-sm leading-relaxed">
<i>“Mi corazón quedó partido en dos geografías”</i>, she writes, and in that sentence the experience of many migrants is recognized: loving across distance, holding on with courage, and moving forward with gratitude.
    </p>
    <p class="px-4 py-2 text-primary text-sm leading-relaxed">
      We invite you to read <i>“Al otro lado del mundo”</i>, a story that connects us, represents us, and reminds us that although the migrant journey is not easy, it is also full of meaning, learning, and humanity.
    </p>
    <p class="px-4 py-2 text-primary text-sm leading-relaxed ">
      <a href="/docs/Al_otro_lado_del_mundo_Maria_A_Olarte.pdf" class="text-navprimary flex flex-row gap-x-2" target="_blank">
        <img src="https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/e/notoemoji/16.0/1f4d6/72.png" width="16px" >Full story: Al otro lado del mundo
      </a>
    </p>
    <p class="px-4 py-2 text-primary text-sm leading-relaxed flex flex-row gap-x-2">
      <img src="https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/e/notoemoji/16.0/270d_fe0f/72.png" width="16px" alt="">Author: María Alejandra Olarte Molina
    </p>
